  m_Name: Hemlock Wolly Adelgid
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  bugName: Hemlock Wolly Adelgid
  info: "The Hemlock Wolly Adelgid is a small insect native to East Asia that feeds
    by sucking the sap from Hemlock and Spruce Trees. \n\nThe insect may also inject
    a toxin while feeding. The resulting desiccation causes the tree to lose needles
    and prevent new growth.\n\n While not a serious pest in its native range due
    to the presence of natural predators which manage populations, in eastern North
    America it is a destructive pest that threatens the eastern hemlock and the Carolina
    hemlock."
  bugImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e744fa4f017d908459e30403178f1dd3, type: 3}
